 "name": "snake_costume_python",
 "description": "Zipped felt tube suit from the neck to the ankles over Doug's rig, both legs in one flared tube (wide enough for walk1/walk2 and arms_up stances), front zipper with pull tab, stitched edges, small arm holes at the shoulders so Doug's own arms show, open neck collar (head, face and red cap fully visible), felt tail trailing on the ground behind him to (-262,+148). Deadpan felt, no snake face. Poses: stand, point, hands_hips, thumbs_up, shrug, arms_up, wave, walk1/walk2. Pose `cower` drops Doug's head ~40 units: place the suit at y + 40*scale for cower or the collar overlaps his chin. Reticulated python suit: fatter, wider tube (x1.3), gold-tan #c9a24a felt with a black net pattern of grey-tan diamonds and small white spots. Anchor = Doug's hips (0,0), Doug scale-1 units (neck y -150, feet y +152); list after Doug at the same x/y/scale/flip. ",
